//! A fuzzer-found, minimised Parquet reproducer for the arrow-ipc embedded-
//! schema panic (#52), committed **as source** (a `const &[u8]`), not as an
//! opaque binary blob — the repo "no committed binary blob" convention.
//!
//! # Provenance
//!
//! `fuzz_bundle_readback` produced a crash that `cargo fuzz tmin` minimised to
//! these bytes (via `fuzz_parquet_feed`). Before the #52 hardening, feeding
//! them to `ParquetFeed::open` / `read_bundle` **panicked** inside
//! `arrow-ipc` (`unimplemented!("Type NONE not supported")` in
//! `get_data_type`, convert.rs:514): a Parquet footer may embed a malformed
//! `ARROW:schema` IPC flatbuffer, which the reader parsed eagerly. The fix
//! opens the reader with `ArrowReaderOptions::with_skip_arrow_metadata(true)`
//! at both call sites, so the embedded schema is ignored and the malformed
//! bytes now yield a TYPED `BacktestError` (never a panic).
//!
//! Faithful in-Rust synthesis of a NONE-typed flatbuffer field is impractical
//! (arrow's own writer will not emit one), so the minimised reproducer is
//! embedded verbatim — deterministic, reviewable, source-pinned. The exact
//! bytes are irrelevant beyond "this is a Parquet file whose embedded arrow
//! schema is malformed"; the permanent regression is the no-panic assertion
//! in `tests/security.rs`.
//!
//! sha256 = d9291c0f8b487431083ffb7326ed2a81d1c6846fdc44e536ed890e975e2cb9ba
//! length = 3980 bytes

